 "title": "Pathogenicity and Secreted Proteins in Fungal Interactions",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the interactions between various fungal organisms, including Alternaria, A. brassicicola, and Papiliotrema, and their secreted proteins. Ab0920a, an effector of A. brassicicola, secretes the protein Bax. DoMYB102 activates DoUGT71K2, which is expressed in D. officinale. The pathogenicity of Alternaria is linked to A. brassicicola, and Papiliotrema is associated with PDA, which also has a growth characteristic in Papiliotrema flavescens. The RNA method is authored by C.J. Siddique and involves D. officinale. High-yield strain 31.1 has higher coverage than low-yield strain 12.1.",
